Writer keeps a DOCX TOC's field end where Word puts it

A table of contents in a block content control (Word's "Automatic
Table") gets a heading, so the importer builds its section from the
content control's start. Two cases still came out wrong (Ely R15.11h):

- Body text after the field end, in the same paragraph, stayed inside
  the index section. The export then wrote it inside the TOC field,
  where Word's next "Update Table" deletes it. The importer now notes
  where in the paragraph the field ended, and how many objects were
  anchored there. Once the paragraph is finished, any text or new
  anchored object after that point leaves the section: the
  paragraph is split there if the last entry precedes the end, and the
  rest is moved with SwNodes::MoveNodes, which keeps the node, so marks
  and positions in it survive. An empty end paragraph stays in the
  index, as before.
- An inline content control inside an entry cleared the "in a content
  control" state at its end, so the importer deleted the field end's
  own empty paragraph and the end landed in the last entry. A separate
  flag, cleared only at a block content control's end and at the TOC's
  end, keeps that paragraph.
- That kept paragraph then closed the TOC's content control before it.
  An inline content control's end read the shared "outside a paragraph"
  flag, which only some properties set, so an alias-only control kept
  the outer block's value and its end was deferred to the next
  paragraph as a block end. An inline end is now always a run end.

The move only happens if the paragraph is still the section's last
node when it finishes; otherwise the import goes on as before, with a
warning.

